{"id":"8e566080a7b76bc9b80d4ba6c2a09807ff6e7c7f","axis":"silent","repo":"mongodb/mongo","sha":"8e566080a7b76bc9b80d4ba6c2a09807ff6e7c7f","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"src/mongo/db/index_builds/index_build_attempts.cpp","lines":["@@ -298,11 +298,6 @@ bool checkWithinAttemptLimit(OperationContext* opCtx,","                              const std::string& ident,","                              ResumeIndexInfo& resumeInfo,","                              bool plannedHandoff) {","-    // Draining is exempt so unrelated failovers during a long drain do not abort the build.","-    if (resumeInfo.getPhase() == IndexBuildPhaseEnum::kDrainWrites) {","-        return true;","-    }","-","     const int limit = gMaxIndexBuildAttemptsAfterUncleanShutdown.load();","     const auto prevResumesWithoutProgress = resumeInfo.getResumesWithoutProgress();","     // The first unplanned resume establishes a baseline at 0. Later unplanned resumes without"],"additions":0,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/mongo/db/index_builds/index_build_attempts.h","lines":["@@ -72,8 +72,7 @@ namespace primary_driven {","  * Checks the primary-driven build's resume count against maxIndexBuildAttemptsAfterUncleanShutdown.","  * Returns false if over the limit. Resumes identified as planned handoffs do not increment the","  * count. Otherwise, attempts to persist the count with majority write concern and updates","- * 'resumeInfo' on success. Builds already in the drain phase are exempt from checking or recording","- * the count.","+ * 'resumeInfo' on success.","  */"," bool checkWithinAttemptLimit(OperationContext* opCtx,","                              const DatabaseName& dbName,"],"additions":1,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/mongo/db/index_builds/index_build_attempts_test.cpp","lines":["@@ -215,7 +215,8 @@ class PrimaryDrivenIndexBuildAttemptsTest : public CatalogTestFixture {","         CatalogTestFixture::tearDown();","     }"," ","-    ResumeIndexInfo setUpRegisteredBuild(size_